        {
          "linkId": "dry-ed",
          "text": "Dry eye is a chronic surface problem, not a one-drop cure. Twice-daily warm compresses (8–10 minutes) plus lid hygiene help oil glands. Use preservative-free tears when screens or AC flare symptoms. Point vents away from your face. 20-20-20 blinks. Stop sleeping in contact lenses. Return sooner for increasing redness, light sensitivity, or vision drop.",
          "type": "display"
        },
